---
import {
  architecturePaths,
  sparcConstraints,
  sparcIngestion,
  sparcNumbers,
} from '../../data/sparc';
---

<section id="sparc">
  <h2>SPARC</h2>
  <p class="secondary">
    Sole engineer, within STARI · Rust backend, Nuxt 4 web app, infrastructure
  </p>
  <p>
    Sensor Platform for Academic Research and Community. In production since January 2026 on two ULB
    campuses, used by a research center (CIREM) and ULB's infrastructure department.
    {sparcNumbers}
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The problem:</strong> research and campus teams need reliable sensor data, but devices
    speak different protocols and no team should have to run its own pipeline.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://sparc.ulb.be">sparc.ulb.be</a>
  </p>

  <h3>Constraints</h3>
  <ul>
    {sparcConstraints.map((constraint) => (
      <li>{constraint}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h3>Write and read paths</h3>
  <figure>
    {import.meta.env.DEV && (
      <div class="todo">TODO: the actual SPARC architecture diagram (image to be supplied)</div>
    )}
    {architecturePaths.map((path) => (
      <>
        <p>
          <strong>{path.label}</strong>
        </p>
        <ol>
          {path.nodes.map((node) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{node.name}</strong>: {node.description}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </>
    ))}
    <figcaption>
      Around it: Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring, threshold alerts by email, asynchronous CSV
      exports.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3>How data gets in</h3>
  <dl>
    {sparcIngestion.map((item) => (
      <>
        <dt>{item.name}</dt>
        <dd>{item.description}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>
</section>
